//@version=6
// ============================================================================
// RXWLES DIRECTION CALL  v2.3
//
// CORRECTION FIRST. Every figure quoted in v1.2 through v1.6 was produced by a
// backtest that reconstructed the VWAP anchored at midnight New York from
// hlc3. This chart's VWAP is session-anchored - the exported column resets at
// 18:00 NY in 54 of 59 sessions - and sourced from the high. The two series
// disagree by a median of $7.13 and by as much as $111.65. Every VWAP-based
// conclusion had to be re-tested, and two of them reversed.
//
//   DIRECTION  04:00 NY, whichever zone is closer.
//   NO TRADE   if a position is still open, if the 2.0 zone already went before
//              the call, or if the 9pm range is over the limit.
//   STOP LEVEL the 9pm box edge plus a $1.00 buffer.
//   ENTRY      a VWAP tap before 14:00 NY. Both are fixed, not inputs.
//   CANCEL     if the box stop level or the zone is reached before the fill.
//   TARGET     just inside the far edge of the zone - 2.5 R less 0.05.
//   EXIT       target or stop. No time exit, no break-even.
//
// What reversed. The 9pm box was a co-equal entry alongside the VWAP because
// the broken series said it cost nothing to add. Against the real VWAP it
// dilutes rather than adds, so the box entry is gone and the VWAP tap is the
// only trigger. The entry cutoff moves from 11:00 to 14:00, which is a clean
// step rather than a spike - 10:00 through 13:00 all give +32.7 R, 14:00
// through 16:00 all give +34.8 R.
//
// Both are hard-coded in v1.8 rather than offered as settings. That is a
// deliberate narrowing: the alternatives below were all measured and all lost,
// so the only thing an input would buy is a way to set it wrong.
//
// 59 sessions of 15m gold, measured against the chart's own VWAP:
//
//   entry                         n    W/L    win%   PF   avgRR   avgR    totR
//   VWAP tap, cutoff 14:00       31  18W/13L  58.1%  3.68  3.16   +1.12  +34.8
//   VWAP tap, cutoff 11:00       31  17W/14L  54.8%  3.33  3.28   +1.05  +32.7
//   first of either (v1.6)       35  19W/16L  54.3%  2.68  2.34   +0.77  +26.9
//   box touch only               34  18W/16L  52.9%     -  2.44   +0.76  +25.9
//   close with VWAP behind       42  28W/14L  66.7%  2.90  1.68   +0.63  +26.7
//
// The close-with-VWAP-behind entry is the one genuine alternative and it is
// worth knowing about even though it is not in here: it converts nothing, it
// adds ten sessions the tap entry misses of which nine win, and it drops three
// that were losses. It pays for that with a wider stop, $32.23 against $23.30,
// so the money comes out the same while the hit rate goes up twelve points. If
// you ever want it, it is one line - enter at the close of the first bar that
// closes with the VWAP behind price, instead of on the tap.
//
// Stops, same 59 sessions:
//
//   behind the 9pm box           35  19W/16L  54.3%  PF 2.68  max DD 4.0 R
//   60 pips beyond the VWAP      36  11W/25L  30.6%  PF 2.14  max DD 6.5 R
//
// The VWAP stop reaches a similar total on a third of the dollar risk, but a
// 30.6% win rate with a six-loss streak is a different thing to hold. 30 pips
// - the tightest asked about - goes 6W/29L for -8.5 R, because $3.00 sits
// inside a single 15m bar's range more often than not.
//
// Left out on purpose, all re-tested against the real VWAP and all still dead:
// break-even part-way to target (every level from 40% to 90% loses), any time
// exit, turning off the one-position lock, and a range filter anywhere other
// than $40. The minimum-RR floor now measures positive but wobbles - none
// +34.8, 2.0 +37.0, 2.5 +35.4, 3.0 +39.5 - which is noise on 31 trades, not a
// setting.
//
// One known difference between this script and the backtest: here a position
// is managed from the bar after it fills, so the entry bar cannot stop you
// out. The backtest assumed the worse case for tap entries. It barely matters
// at a $23 stop and matters a lot at a $3 one.
//
// ONE CHANGE IN v1.9: the target moves from the near edge of the zone to the
// far one, 2.0 R to 2.5 R. It is the only change here because it is the only
// one with a mechanism behind it rather than a number.
//
//   config                          n    W/L    win%   PF    avgR    totR
//   v1.8: 2.0 edge                 31  18W/13L  58.1%  3.68  +1.12  +34.8
//   v1.9: 2.5 edge                 32  18W/14L  56.2%  4.18  +1.39  +44.5
//
//   split           2.0 edge    2.5 edge
//   first half       +16.5 R     +21.6 R    (8W/6L either way)
//   second half      +18.3 R     +22.9 R
//
// Max drawdown stays at 3.0 R. It holds in both halves independently, and it
// peaks at exactly the far edge and falls away past it - 2.75 drops to +35.1 R
// - which is what you would expect if the zone is a real destination rather
// than a fitted number.
//
// The stop buffer was measured in the same pass and left alone. It costs money
// on paper - the record is 18W/14L at every width from $0.00 to $3.00 while
// the total falls +47.8 R to +30.2 R - but the reason is that no winning trade
// ever came within $2.54 of the box edge, so the wick-and-recover event a
// buffer exists for never once arose. That makes it untested, not useless, and
// $1.00 stays until a bigger sample can rule on it.
//
// Tried in the same pass and rejected: delaying the entry past the call bar
// (every delay loses), a minimum RR to enter (raises PF to 4.22, cuts total R
// to +29.0), a dollar cap on risk (all worse), and trading one direction only
// (shorts 60% and +21.6 R, longs 42.9% and +10.2 R - but both make money and
// 14 longs decide nothing).
//
// v2.0 ADDS ONE THING: the take profit rests a twentieth of a box inside the
// far edge rather than on it. The argument is execution, not statistics - an
// order sitting on the exact edge of a level every other chart draws is at the
// back of that queue.
//
//   target                          n    W/L    win%   PF    totR
//   on the 2.50 edge (v1.9)        32  18W/14L  56.2%  4.18  +44.5
//   0.05 R inside it (v2.0)        32  19W/13L  59.4%  4.57  +46.5
//
// 2026-08-18 is the case that prompted it. Price came within 8 cents of the
// untouched edge, turned, and stopped out for -1.00 R. Worse, the position was
// still open at the next morning's call, so the one-position lock skipped a
// session that went on to run. A 0.05 R pull-in banks that trade at 21:00 the
// same evening and hands the next day back. One change, both problems.
//
// Softening the lock directly was tried and does not work: unlimited positions
// gives +42.3 R, letting a second through once the open one clears +0.5 R
// gives +43.5 R, and every threshold at +1.0 R or above never triggers. The
// blockage is worth fixing at its cause, not by loosening the rule that caught
// it.
//
// Anything from 0.02 to 0.25 R rescues the same trade - the W/L is 19W/13L
// across that whole band - so the size is not fitted, only the amount of the
// other winners you hand back. Split: first half +21.1 R against +21.6, second
// half +25.4 R against +22.9. It costs a little on every winner and rescues
// one loss, and the rescue happened in the second half.
//
// v2.1 ADDS THE OPPOSING-CALL EXIT. The next day's direction call closes an
// open position that disagrees with it - but only one that is not yet in
// profit. A winner is left alone.
//
//   handling of a call that arrives with a trade open    n   W/L    PF   totR   DD
//   skip the call, keep the trade (v2.0)                32  19W/13L 4.57 +46.5 3.0
//   cut every opposing call                             35  20W/15L 4.05 +41.6 3.0
//   cut only while the trade is under water (v2.1)      34  20W/14L 4.72 +47.1 2.8
//
// Cutting every opposing call fails on one trade: 2026-07-28 was closed for
// +0.74 R with a 5.23 R target still live, and that single decision costs more
// than the three saves it made. Restricting the cut to positions under water
// keeps the saves and leaves the winners alone. Better in both halves - first
// +21.2 against +21.1, second +25.8 against +25.4 - though the margin is thin.
//
// Anything from 0.00 to +0.50 R gives the same result. At +1.00 R it starts
// cutting winners and collapses back to +41.6 R.
//
// The lock stays on. The six sessions it discarded over the sample were 1W/4L
// worth -2.2 R, so it is filtering rather than costing, and three separate
// tests - defer until close, unlimited positions, cut every opposing call -
// all came back worse.
//
// v2.2 IS A FULL RE-SWEEP, every knob moved one at a time against the finished
// rule set rather than against whatever the rule set looked like when that knob
// was first tested. Everything held at its existing value except the stop
// buffer, which moves $1.00 -> $0.50.
//
//   knob            values tried                       best      kept
//   call hour       3 / 4 / 5 / 6                      4         4
//   entry cutoff    10 / 11 / 12 / 14 / 16             14 = 16   14
//   zone edge       2.0 / 2.25 / 2.4 / 2.5 / 2.6/2.75  2.5       2.5
//   target pull-in  0 / .02 / .05 / .10 / .20          0.02      0.05
//   stop buffer     0 / .25 / .50 / 1.00 / 2.00        0.00      0.50
//   range filter    off / 35 / 40 / 45 / 50            40        40
//   cut-below       0 / .25 / .50 / 1.00               .25 = .50 0.25
//   break-even      off / 40% / 50% / 75%              off       off
//   lock            on / off                           on        on
//   opposing cut    on / off                           on        on
//
// Two places where the measured optimum was not taken, both for the same
// reason - a backtest cannot see the spread. The 0.02 R pull-in is 64 cents on
// a $32 box, inside the spread on gold, so 0.05 stays. And the $0.00 buffer
// scores +50.2 R but drops a winner and lifts the drawdown to 3.0 R, where
// $0.50 keeps 20W/14L at 2.8 R.
//
//   FINAL: 34 trades  20W/14L  58.8%  PF 4.85  +1.43 R avg  +48.7 R  DD 2.8 R
//
// 34 trades. The range filter rests on 7 observations. XAUUSD only, costs are
// still not modelled, and the split-sample check is two halves of one quarter.
// ============================================================================

indicator("RXWLES Direction Call", "DirCall", overlay = true,
     max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500)

const string TZ = "America/New_York"

// Hard-coded, not inputs. These two are the version: a VWAP tap, before 14:00
// New York. Measured 18W/13L, PF 3.68, +34.8 R over 59 sessions of 15m gold,
// against 19W/16L and PF 2.68 for the box-inclusive entry it replaced. The
// cutoff is a step and not a spike - 10:00 to 13:00 all give +32.7 R and
// 14:00 to 16:00 all give +34.8 R.
const int cutHour = 14

//=============================================================================
// METHOD
//=============================================================================

srcHour  = input.int(21, "Source candle hour (NY)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Method",
     tooltip = "Must match RXWLES PRO's Enigma Source Hour.")
readHour = input.int(4,  "Direction read hour (NY)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "Method")
lvl1     = input.float(2.5, "Zone edge used as the target (R)", step = 0.05,
     group = "Method",
     tooltip = "RXWLES PRO draws the zone as 2.0 to 2.5 R. Aiming at the far edge "
             + "rather than the near one measures better and there is a reason: of "
             + "the 34 sessions that reach 2.0, 30 carry on to 2.5 - 88.2% "
             + "follow-through. You give up a ninth of your winners to be paid a "
             + "quarter more on each. 2.5 gives 18W/14L, PF 4.18, +44.5 R against "
             + "2.0's 18W/13L, PF 3.68, +34.8 R, and it holds in both halves of "
             + "the sample. Past 2.5 it falls away - 2.75 drops to +35.1 R, "
             + "because that is asking price to leave the zone rather than reach it.")
tgtPull  = input.float(0.05, "    take profit this far inside the edge (R)", step = 0.01,
     minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, group = "Method",
     tooltip = "Do not rest the order on the exact edge of a level every other "
             + "chart draws. You are at the back of that queue. Pulling it a "
             + "twentieth of a box inside - $1.60 on a $32 box, about 16 pips - "
             + "takes 18W/14L and PF 4.18 to 19W/13L and PF 4.57. On 2026-08-18 "
             + "the low came within 8 cents of the untouched edge, reversed and "
             + "stopped out for -1.00 R; a 0.05 R pull-in banks it at 21:00 the "
             + "same evening, which also frees the next day's call that the "
             + "one-position lock would otherwise have skipped. Anything from "
             + "0.02 to 0.25 R rescues the same trade - past that you are just "
             + "paying more of the winners away.")
vwAnc    = input.string("Session", "VWAP anchor", group = "Method",
     options = ["Session", "Midnight NY (lane open)"],
     tooltip = "Session is what TradingView's own VWAP indicator uses - pick this "
             + "and the line sits exactly on top of yours. Midnight NY was the old "
             + "v1.3 behaviour and does not match the built-in VWAP.")
vwSrc    = input.source(high, "VWAP source", group = "Method",
     tooltip = "Set to match the Source in your own VWAP indicator's settings. "
             + "High is what yours uses. On 59 sessions of 15m gold, high fills "
             + "23W/12L +0.91 R against hlc3's 22W/12L +0.86 R - a high-sourced "
             + "VWAP sits above the hlc3 one, so long pullbacks reach it sooner.")

stopMode = input.string("Behind the 9pm box", "Stop placement", group = "Stop & target",
     options = ["Behind the 9pm box", "Beyond the VWAP"],
     tooltip = "One or the other, never both. The box stop measures 19W/16L, PF "
             + "2.68, max drawdown 4.0 R. The VWAP stop at 60 pips reaches a "
             + "similar +28.4 R on a third of the dollar risk, but on an 11W/25L "
             + "record - a 30.6% win rate, a 6.5 R drawdown and a six-loss streak.")
bufD     = input.float(0.50, "    box stop: buffer beyond the box ($)", step = 0.10,
     minval = 0.0, group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "The buffer costs money and never once saved a trade. Across 59 "
             + "sessions the record is 18W/14L at every buffer from $0.00 to "
             + "$3.00 - identical - while the total falls from +47.8 R to +30.2 R "
             + "as the stop widens. $0.00 measures best and holds in both halves. "
             + "Re-swept against the full v2.2 rule set: $2.00 gives +44.1 R, "
             + "$1.00 +47.1, $0.50 +48.7, $0.25 +49.3 and $0.00 +50.2. But the "
             + "two tightest drop a winner and push the drawdown from 2.8 R to "
             + "3.0, so $0.50 is the pick - it keeps 20W/14L and the lower "
             + "drawdown while banking most of the gain. It also leaves a little "
             + "cushion against the spread taking a stop that rests exactly on a "
             + "level everyone can see, which no backtest can measure. $0.00 is "
             + "worth +1.5 R more if you disagree.")
stopPips = input.int(80, "    VWAP stop: pips beyond the VWAP", minval = 1,
     group = "Stop & target")
pipSize  = input.float(0.10, "    what one pip is worth ($)", step = 0.01, minval = 0.0001,
     group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "0.10 for gold, so 30 pips is $3.00 and 80 pips is $8.00.")
useBE    = input.bool(false, "Break-even once price is part-way to target",
     group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "Re-measured against the 2.5 target, where it is a much closer "
             + "call than it was against 2.0. Off: 18W/14L, PF 4.18, +44.5 R, "
             + "3.0 R drawdown. Armed at 50%: 15W/9L/9BE, PF 5.70, +42.3 R, "
             + "2.0 R drawdown - five losses become scratches, but three winners "
             + "do too, and those three were worth 7.2 R between them. Anywhere "
             + "from 40% to 60% gives exactly the same result, so it is a wide "
             + "plateau rather than a lucky number. Fewer losses and a third off "
             + "the drawdown for 2.2 R. It stays off because total R is a coin "
             + "flip between the two halves of the sample - the first half prefers "
             + "it, the second does not - while the loss count and the profit "
             + "factor improve in both.")
beFrac   = input.float(50.0, "    at this % of the entry-to-target distance",
     step = 5.0, minval = 1.0, maxval = 99.0, group = "Stop & target")
maxDays  = input.int(5, "Give up on an unresolved trade after (days)", minval = 1, maxval = 20,
     group = "Stop & target",
     tooltip = "A safety valve, not a strategy rule. Only one trade in the sample "
             + "ever reached it.")

lockOne  = input.bool(true, "One position at a time - skip the call while open",
     group = "Filters",
     tooltip = "The six sessions this discarded were 1W/4L worth -2.2 R, so it is "
             + "filtering rather than costing. Letting them all through measures "
             + "+40.4 R against +46.5 R. A call arriving while a trade is open is "
             + "a call on a day whose box has usually already been breached.")
cutOpp   = input.bool(true, "Close a losing trade when the next call opposes it",
     group = "Filters",
     tooltip = "The new day's direction call doubles as an exit, but only for a "
             + "position that is not yet in profit - a winner is left alone to "
             + "run. Cutting every opposing call regardless measures +41.6 R, "
             + "because on 2026-07-28 it closed a 5.23 R winner for +0.74 R. "
             + "Cutting only the ones under water gives 20W/14L, PF 4.72, "
             + "+47.1 R and a 2.8 R drawdown, against 19W/13L, PF 4.57, +46.5 R "
             + "and 3.0 R for skipping. Better in both halves of the sample, "
             + "though only just. It also frees the day the closed trade was "
             + "blocking.")
cutBelow = input.float(0.25, "    only if it is below this many R", step = 0.05,
     minval = -1.0, maxval = 2.0, group = "Filters",
     tooltip = "0.00 through 0.50 all measure the same. At +1.00 R it starts "
             + "cutting winners and collapses back to +41.6 R.")
useRngF  = input.bool(true, "Skip days with an oversized 9pm range", group = "Filters",
     tooltip = "Sessions at or above the limit went 1W/6L.")
maxRng   = input.float(40.0, "    range limit ($)", step = 1.0, minval = 1.0, group = "Filters")

//=============================================================================
// APPEARANCE
//=============================================================================

f_style(string s) =>
    s == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : s == "Dotted" ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid

f_size(string s) =>
    s == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : s == "Normal" ? size.normal : s == "Large" ? size.large :
     s == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.small

f_cfPos(string s) =>
    s == "Bottom left"   ? position.bottom_left   : s == "Bottom centre" ? position.bottom_center :
     s == "Top right"    ? position.top_right     : s == "Top left"      ? position.top_left :
     s == "Middle right" ? position.middle_right  : s == "Middle left"   ? position.middle_left :
     position.bottom_right

// The measured hit rate for a reading. Grid = lopsidedness x range ratio.
f_cfHit(float raw, int q, bool grid) =>
    float h = na
    if grid and q > 0
        int c = raw < 0.10 ? 1 : raw < 0.20 ? 2 : raw < 0.30 ? 3 : 4
        h := q == 1 ? (c == 1 ? 55.9 : c == 2 ? 69.0 : c == 3 ? 76.8 : 85.9) :
             q == 2 ? (c == 1 ? 58.8 : c == 2 ? 69.0 : c == 3 ? 76.5 : 79.5) :
             q == 3 ? (c == 1 ? 60.4 : c == 2 ? 70.5 : c == 3 ? 79.8 : 94.3) :
                      (c == 1 ? 68.3 : c == 2 ? 75.8 : c == 3 ? 83.6 : 92.6)
    else
        h := raw < 0.05 ? 57.7 : raw < 0.10 ? 64.0 : raw < 0.15 ? 68.2 :
             raw < 0.20 ? 74.8 : raw < 0.25 ? 78.4 : raw < 0.35 ? 81.3 : 94.9
    h

f_shape(string s, int dir) =>
    s == "Arrow (auto)"          ? (dir > 0 ? label.style_arrowup : label.style_arrowdown) :
     s == "Speech bubble (auto)" ? (dir > 0 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down) :
     s == "Circle"               ? label.style_circle :
     s == "Square"               ? label.style_square :
     s == "Diamond"              ? label.style_diamond :
     s == "Flag"                 ? label.style_flag :
     s == "Cross"                ? label.style_cross :
     s == "X"                    ? label.style_xcross :
     s == "Text only"            ? label.style_none :
     s == "Emoji"                ? label.style_none :
     (dir > 0 ? label.style_triangleup : label.style_triangledown)

dShow  = input.bool(true, "Show direction marker", group = "Direction marker")
dShape = input.string("Triangle (auto)", "Shape", group = "Direction marker",
     options = ["Triangle (auto)", "Arrow (auto)", "Speech bubble (auto)", "Circle", "Square",
                "Diamond", "Flag", "Cross", "X", "Text only", "Emoji"])
dUpEmo = input.string("🔼", "Emoji up", inline = "de", group = "Direction marker")
dDnEmo = input.string("🔽", "down", inline = "de", group = "Direction marker")
dSize  = input.string("Tiny", "Size", group = "Direction marker",
     options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"])
dUpCol = input.color(#26a69a, "Up", inline = "dc", group = "Direction marker")
dDnCol = input.color(#ef5350, "Down", inline = "dc", group = "Direction marker")
dTrans = input.int(35, "Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = "Direction marker")
dOff   = input.float(0.20, "Offset from the candle (R)", step = 0.05, minval = 0.0,
     group = "Direction marker")
dSkip  = input.bool(true, "Mark calls skipped because a trade is open",
     group = "Direction marker")
dSkipCol = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 40), "    skip colour", group = "Direction marker")

eShow  = input.bool(true, "Show entry marker", group = "Entry marker")
eShape = input.string("Arrow (auto)", "Shape", group = "Entry marker",
     options = ["Triangle (auto)", "Arrow (auto)", "Speech bubble (auto)", "Circle", "Square",
                "Diamond", "Flag", "Cross", "X", "Text only", "Emoji"])
eUpEmo = input.string("🎯", "Emoji up", inline = "ee", group = "Entry marker")
eDnEmo = input.string("🎯", "down", inline = "ee", group = "Entry marker")
eSize  = input.string("Normal", "Size", group = "Entry marker",
     options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"])
eUpCol = input.color(#00e676, "Up", inline = "ec", group = "Entry marker")
eDnCol = input.color(#ff1744, "Down", inline = "ec", group = "Entry marker")
eTrans = input.int(0, "Transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = "Entry marker")
eText  = input.string("RR", "Text", options = ["None", "Price", "RR", "Price + RR"],
     group = "Entry marker")
eTxtCol = input.color(color.white, "Text colour", group = "Entry marker")
eOff   = input.float(0.45, "Offset from the candle (R)", step = 0.05, minval = 0.0,
